{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a08c81-93da-7488-98a6-e934be891f53","session_id":"01a08c80-51fc-7e4d-8c44-75c5d8fe8dd6","message":{"id":"01a08c8193da748898a6e9326de8926b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now have a very complete picture. Let me get a few more key files:\n1. The ctgov_fetch tests to confirm if they use real network or just transport fixtures\n2. Look at the policy.yaml file (SourcePolicy)\n3. Check whether capability_preflight actually does live probing\n4. Look at the PageRegistry entry for fetching\n\nI should also check fixtures to see if real data is used and verify the question A producer question is settled.\n\nLet me consolidate findings now and write the plan file. I have enough evidence to be definitive:\n\n**Question A:**\n1. `SemanticGroupingProposal` definition: `src/ci_workflow/reports/b/semantic_grouping.py:34-61` - has only status: Literal[\"proposal\"] (literal type, only \"proposal\"). NO approved/issued state on the proposal itself.\n2. Producer: NO real producer in src. Only tests construct them with `producer_id=\"synthetic-model\"` (test_semantic_grouping_proposals.py:35). The renderer just reads proposals that come in via the data payload.\n3. Consumer: `src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/report_b.py:2883` calls `proposed_semantic_buckets` which CONSUMES proposals to constrain/combine groups; also `_semantic_group_key` at line 2873 computes grouping independently. The proposals do affect grouping.\n4. `review_issuer`: `src/ci_workflow/application/review_issuer.py:330 (issue_review_receipt)`. `scientific_review_transition`: `src/ci_workflow/application/scientific_review_transition.py` - has RENDERED_UNREVIEWED → SCIENTIFICALLY_REVIEWED_RENDERED_CANDIDATE (lines 79-82). This is for the WHOLE PORTAL artifact, not for individual proposals. cli.py:780 invokes this in production via `_review_issue_handler`. There's NO proposal-specific transition.\n5. `clinical_unit`: ABSENT. `time_policy`: ABSENT (only `time_window_band`). `unresolved_due_to_route`: present in report_b.py:147. `not_applicable`: present via SourceApplicability / FactDisclosureState.\n\n**Question B:**\n1. Connectors:\n- clinicaltrials_gov.py: 353 lines, pure validation, URL builders, record parser. NO fetching.\n- pubmed.py: 300 lines, has `build_pubmed_nct_search_url` (line 104) and `parse_pubmed_efetch_xml` (line 125). NO fetching.\n- regulators.py: 348 lines, pure validation. NO fetching.\n- company.py: 168 lines, pure validation. NO fetching.\n- china_registries.py: 672 lines, pure validation, URL builders. NO fetching.\n- authoritative_wechat.py: 248 lines, pure validation. NO fetching.\n- ctgov_fetch.py: 288 lines, REAL implementation - uses urllib.request.\n\n2. CT.gov connector real fetch support: `ctgov_fetch.py:101 fetch_ctgov_condition` - REAL network via `urllib.request.Request`. Single query shape: by condition (`query.cond`). NO by-indication by-sponsor by-intervention by-NCT. Pagination supported via nextPageToken.\n\n3. Code paths:\n- Historical/versioned record retrieval: `planner.py:132 assess_historical_source` is just cutoff assessment. NO actual historical retrieval. `ctgov_fetch.py:94 temporal_scope: Literal[\"current_records\"] = \"current_records\"` - explicitly current only.\n- Data freshness: `fetch_ctgov_condition` does live fetch (returns `acquired_at`), but the planner just uses current.\n- Publication end-to-end: pubmed.py exists but no execution flow that uses it for end-to-end acquisition (only XML parsing helpers).\n- OCR: ABSENT (no OCR code found).\n- yaozh browser adapters: `application/yaozh_access.py` - access tracking only. NO browser fetching. The v1 spec says no browser adapters per AGENTS.md.\n\n4. Planner: `src/ci_workflow/sources/planner.py` is purely a state-machine model class (`RouteProgress`), NOT an executable planner that enforces routes. It exposes `record_attempt`, `complete` methods but no actual route plan. The SourcePolicy in policy.py has required_global_baseline/required_for_china bools. There is no enforcement in the planner; enforcement seems to be in `research_package.py:1019-1020` (`required_route_ids`).\n\n5. Tests: I need to check the ctgov_fetch tests - they're a mix of synthetic transport tests. Let me verify the indication tests.\n\nLet me write the plan file with all these findings. Actually, I have enough, let me do the final write up and ExitPlanMode.\n\nBut first I should double-check one or two critical items:\n- Verify fixture data isn't pretending to be live\n- Look at the research_package.py for required_route_ids enforcement\n- Look at the integration test for ctgov_fetch","signature":""}],"model":"minimax-m3","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_02_7faHW2LQzop1uyMQUW6r9666","_requestId":"01a08c80d6917d96bda67b4c7a4cb76d","_messageId":"01a08c8193da748898a6e9326de8926b","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a08c80d6917d96bda67b4c7a4cb76d","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a08c8193da748898a6e9326de8926b","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a08c8193da748898a6e9326de8926b","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a08c81-93da-7488-98a6-e934be891f53","traceparent":"00-a4b4af999c08dd6458b96ec034bb4fe0-e2f7c4948accacf5-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a08c80-51fc-7e4d-8c44-75c5d8fe8dd6,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a08c8052637ef99d54eb1364f5e9f1"},"__timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:08:26.493Z"}
