{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a08c82-a48a-7275-9bae-4154ba3e106a","session_id":"01a08c80-51fc-7e4d-8c44-75c5d8fe8dd6","message":{"id":"01a08c82a48a72759bae4153b3c8b712","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I don't have access to the Write or ExitPlanMode tools in this session. I'll provide the comprehensive findings directly in this response. The investigation is complete; here are the findings in markdown:\n\n---\n\n# Investigation Findings\n\n## QUESTION A — SemanticGroupingProposal chain (not closed)\n\n### A1. Definition & fields — `SemanticGroupingProposal`\n\n`/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/reports/b/semantic_grouping.py:34-61`\n\n```python\n34→class SemanticGroupingProposal(BaseModel):\n35→    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\", frozen=True)\n36→\n37→    schema_version: Literal[\"1\"] = \"1\"\n38→    status: Literal[\"proposal\"] = \"proposal\"\n39→    proposal_id: str\n40→    row_ids: tuple[str, str]\n41→    row_digests: tuple[str, str]\n42→    compatible: bool\n43→    time_window_compatible: bool = False\n44→    producer_id: str\n45→    rationale_zh: str\n```\n\n- File header (`semantic_grouping.py:1`): `\"Bound model proposals for candidate B views; not an independent acceptance receipt.\"`\n- **No review/issuer/approval state.** `status: Literal[\"proposal\"]` is the ONLY valid status — the schema literally cannot represent `candidate → approved/issued`.\n- `producer_id` is a free-text label, not a state transition or signer.\n- The test file even confirms this: `tests/reports/b/test_semantic_grouping_proposals.py:97` `forged = _proposal(first, second).model_copy(update={\"status\": \"accepted\"})` raises `ValueError` because `status` is locked to `\"proposal\"`.\n\n### A2. Who PRODUCES a proposal at runtime\n\n**No real LLM-backed producer exists in `src/`.** Searches across `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src` for `SemanticGroupingProposal` and `proposed_semantic_buckets` yield only the definition site (`semantic_grouping.py:34`, `:55`, `:91`, `:93`, `:110`, `:112`) and the consumer site in the renderer (`report_b.py:36-37`, `:1177`, `:2868`, `:2883`, etc.). No construction site exists in production code paths.\n\nThe only producers anywhere in the repo are **synthetic test fixtures**:\n\n`tests/reports/b/test_semantic_grouping_proposals.py:26-36`\n```python\n26→    from ci_workflow.reports.b.semantic_grouping import (\n27→        SemanticGroupingProposal,\n28→        semantic_row_digest,\n29→    )\n30→\n31→    return SemanticGroupingProposal(\n32→        proposal_id=\"synthetic-proposal\", row_ids=(first[\"row_id\"], second[\"row_id\"]),\n33→        row_digests=(semantic_row_digest(first), semantic_row_digest(second)),\n34→        compatible=True, rationale_zh=\"同一临床构念，实际时间分别为48与50周。\",\n35→        producer_id=\"synthetic-model\", time_window_compatible=True,\n36→    )\n```\n\n`tests/browser/test_b_semantic_proposals.py` and `tests/reports/b/test_r13_semantic_grouping.py` likewise feed hand-built proposals into the renderer. There is no capability module that constructs `SemanticGroupingProposal`. The application layer (`src/ci_workflow/capabilities/`, `src/ci_workflow/application/`) has no producer.\n\n**Verdict: only stub / test fixtures. No real producer in production code.**\n\n### A3. Who CONSUMES proposals to drive page grouping\n\n`/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/report_b.py`\n\nThe renderer is the sole consumer. Two usage patterns:\n\n**Pattern 1 — proposal-pass-through with its own grouping key.** `report_b.py:2861-2883` (`_cross_trial_groups`):\n```python\n2861→def _cross_trial_groups(\n2862→    records: Sequence[tuple[dict[str, Any], Any]],\n2863→    *,\n2864→    page_id: str,\n2865→    domain: str,\n2866→    include_time: bool,\n2867→    chart_type: str | None = None,\n2868→    semantic_proposals: Sequence[SemanticGroupingProposal] = (),\n2869→) -> tuple[dict[str, Any], ...]:\n2870→    buckets: dict[tuple[str, ...], list[tuple[dict[str, Any], Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n2871→    for item in records:\n2872→        row = item[0]\n2873→        key = _semantic_group_key(row, include_time=include_time)\n...\n2883→    merged = proposed_semantic_buckets(tuple(buckets.values()), semantic_proposals)\n```\nInitial grouping is by `_semantic_group_key` (a deterministic function of the row's `_semantic_policy` fields), then `proposed_semantic_buckets` merges pairs that have a `compatible=True` proposal and the same row identity digest. `_semantic_group_key` does NOT consult the proposal.\n\n**Pattern 2 — descriptive-only veto.** `semantic_grouping.py:118-119`:\n```python\n118→        if descriptive_only and proposal.compatible:\n119→            raise ValueError(\"该域目前仅支持描述性展示，不能接受正向语义裁决提案\")\n```\nBaseline/disposition/matrix pages only accept `compatible=False` proposals (a veto); they do not consume positive adjudication.\n\nThe payload field that carries the proposals into rendering: `report_b.py:1177` `semantic_proposals: tuple[SemanticGroupingProposal, ...] = Field(...)` inside `ReportBPortalData`, populated from incoming data (`report_b.py:2868`, `:2964`, `:2971`, `:2981`, `:3001`, `:3005`, `:3014`, `:3022`, `:3047`, `:3098`, `:3134`, `:3502`, `:3691`, `:3703`, `:3728`).\n\n**Net effect:** proposals can (a) merge pre-bucketed rows when `compatible=True`, (b) veto a candidate grouping, (c) be rejected when row digests drift. They are loaded verbatim from the input — the renderer never *generates* them.\n\n### A4. `review_issuer` & `scientific_review_transition`\n\n`/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/application/review_issuer.py:330` — `issue_review_receipt(...)`. This is the **only** approval/issuance entry point.\n\n`/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/application/scientific_review_transition.py:79-82`:\n```python\n79→RENDERED_UNREVIEWED: Final = \"rendered_unreviewed\"\n80→SCIENTIFICALLY_REVIEWED_RENDERED_CANDIDATE: Final = (\n81→    \"scientifically_reviewed_rendered_candidate\"\n82→)\n```\nThe full transition set in the codebase is a **two-state machine on the portal artifact**, not on proposals.\n\n- `accepted_verdict_from_receipt` (`scientific_review_transition.py:575`) verifies a ScientificReviewReceipt but binds to `ScientificQcCurrentContext` (which references the portal — `project_id`, `report_kind`, `report_object_id`, `candidate_snapshot_id`, `coverage_set_id`, etc.).\n- `promote_rendered_candidate` (`scientific_review_transition.py:646-688`) moves the candidate to `SCIENTIFICALLY_REVIEWED_RENDERED_CANDIDATE` only after the receipt/verdict has bound to the rendered portal bytes.\n\n**There is no function in the codebase that transitions a `SemanticGroupingProposal` from candidate to approved/issued.** The proposal carries no approval state, and the review flow operates on the rendered portal, not on individual semantic proposals.\n\nProduction CLI call sites of `issue_review_receipt` (`cli.py:763-797` `_review_issue_handler`, invoking at `:780`) are reachable through the CLI; production integration of `verify_receipt_issuance` is at `application/run_service.py:2130` (C-report path) and `:2490` (A-report path). These gate the **whole portal**, not semantic proposals.\n\n### A5. P3.1/P3.2/P3.3-P3.5 (clinical_unit / time_policy / unknown / not_applicable / N-A separation)\n\n- `clinical_unit`: ABSENT. Only one hit across the entire repo: `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/packets/2026-09-11-takeover-review/runs/reviewer-b-events.log:140:331` (a reviewer log complaining about its absence). No `ClinicalUnit`, `clinical_unit`, or analogous type in domain/schemas.\n- `time_policy`: only one meaningful mention.\n  - `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/reports/b/contracts.py` (the file referenced in the takeover log) — its actual content is a per-row `time_window_band`/`time_window_compatible` flag (`semantic_grouping.py:43`, `report_b.py:9001`-area time handling). There is **no versioned time-policy class** that carries policy_id + policy_version + effective dates.\n- `unknown` / `unresolved`: present via `semantic_contract.semantic_value_is_unknown` (returned by `_observation` at `semantic_grouping.py:77-86` with default `\"not_reported\"`), and `FactDisclosureState` (`domain/enums.py`) carries an unreported state. There is **no first-class `Unresolved` state class** distinct from \"fact not reported\" or \"route did not run\".\n- `not_applicable` / `N/A`: `SourceApplicability.NOT_APPLICABLE = \"not_applicable\"` (`sources/policy.py:36`), `RouteCompletionState.NOT_APPLICABLE = \"route_not_applicable\"` (`sources/planner.py:15`), and `RouteAttemptResult` includes `AttemptResultClass.NOT_FOUND` (`sources/receipts.py:13`). These are route/result classifications, not clinical-fact classifications. There is **no `not_applicable` value on `ClinicalConstructObservation` or on `FactDisclosureState`.**\n\n---\n\n## QUESTION B — Real source acquisition coverage (P2)\n\n### B1. Connectors — what each connector is\n\nAll seven files in `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/sources/connectors/`:\n\n| File | Approx. lines | Role | Fetching? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `clinicaltrials_gov.py` | 353 | Pydantic record builders (`ClinicalTrialsGovStudyVersion`, `RegistryObservation`, `PublicationCrossReference`), URL/pagination helper (`build_next_page_url`). | **No** — zero `urllib.request`, `requests`, `httpx` imports for fetching. |\n| `pubmed.py` | 300 | `build_pubmed_nct_search_url` (URL builder, :104), `parse_pubmed_efetch_xml` (XML parser, :125), publication classifier (`classify_pubmed_records`). | **No** — only URL construction and parsing. No network code. |\n| `regulators.py` | 348 | `RegulatoryDocumentVersion`, `GuidelineBasis`, `select_current_guideline_basis`, `validate_guideline_lineage`. | **No** — pure validation and a no-op selector. |\n| `company.py` | 168 | `CompanyDisclosureVersion` with maturity classification. | **No** — pure validation. |\n| `china_registries.py` | 672 | `ChinaRegulatoryRecordVersion`, `ChinaDrugTrialVersion`, `ChinaDrugReferenceVersion`, `build_china_trial_search_url`. | **No** — pure validation; URL builders only. |\n| `authoritative_wechat.py` | 248 | `AuthoritativeWechatArticleVersion` with allowlist of 5 accounts (`APPROVED_WECHAT_ACCOUNT_LABELS`). | **No** — pure validation. |\n| `ctgov_fetch.py` | 288 | The single network implementation (see B2). | **Yes** — uses `urllib.request.Request` + `build_opener(_NoRedirect()).open(...)`. |\n\nThe **only network code in the connectors package** is in `ctgov_fetch.py:62-77`:\n```python\n62→def _download(url: str, timeout: float, max_bytes: int) -> HttpPage:\n63→    request = Request(url, headers={\n64→        \"Accept\": \"application/json\", \"User-Agent\": \"CI-Workflow/1.4 public-research\",\n65→    })\n66→    try:\n67→        with build_opener(_NoRedirect()).open(request, timeout=timeout) as response:\n68→            return HttpPage(\n69→                response.status, response.headers.get_content_type(),\n70→                response.read(max_bytes + 1), response.geturl(),\n71→            )\n```\n\n**Verdict:** of the six named connectors the question lists (clinicaltrials_gov, pubmed, regulators, company, china_registries, authoritative_wechat), five are pure data-validation modules with URL builders only; the CT.gov connector ships as a sibling module `ctgov_fetch.py`. PubMed/regulators/company/China/wechat have **no real network implementation** — any \"live\" rows in their shape must originate outside the connector.\n\n### B2. CT.gov connector query shapes\n\n`ctgov_fetch.py:101-211` (`fetch_ctgov_condition`):\n\n```python\n125→    url = API + \"?\" + urlencode({\n126→        \"query.cond\": condition, \"format\": \"json\", \"pageSize\": page_size, \"countTotal\": \"true\",\n127→    })\n```\n\n- **One query shape only:** `query.cond=<condition>` (free-text disease term).\n- The module docstring `ctgov_fetch.py:1-6` is explicit:\n  ```\n  Bounded CT.gov v2 acquisition; pagination completion is not universe closure.\n  This endpoint returns current records, not historical as-of reconstructions.\n  Official interface: https://clinicaltrials.gov/data-api/api\n  No cookies, authentication, alternate hosts or implicit retries are used.\n  ```\n- Pagination: `pageSize` parameter + cursor via `nextPageToken`, paginated by `build_next_page_url` (`clinicaltrials_gov.py:345-352`).\n- **No** by-indication menu, **no** by-sponsor, **no** by-intervention (drug/arm), **no** by-NCT lookup. The CLI exposes only `research-fetch` which takes `args.condition` (`cli.py:498-499`), i.e. free-text condition.\n\n### B3. Code paths\n\n- **Historical / versioned record retrieval: PARTIAL / not closed.** `sources/planner.py:132-200` `assess_historical_source` returns `HistoricalCutoffAssessment` from a pre-existing `SourceVersionRecord` (no fetch). The actual fetcher is hard-limited to current records:\n  `ctgov_fetch.py:93-94`\n  ```python\n  93→    universe_closed: Literal[False] = False\n  94→    temporal_scope: Literal[\"current_records\"] = \"current_records\"\n  ```\n  and `cli.py:528` writes the receipt's own limitation: `\"仅获取当前公开记录；历史版本重建、竞品闭包及独立科学复核尚未完成\"`.\n  No code anywhere implements an as-of historical retrieval from CT.gov (or any other source).\n\n- **Data freshness / dynamic recency consumption: PARTIAL.** `fetch_ctgov_condition` returns `acquired_at` per record (line 84, 222-223) and stores raw bytes via `ContentAddressedStore` (`:184`). Beyond this, there is no dynamic discovery / scheduling / refresh-of-changed-records mechanism in `src/`. `sources/__init__.py` ships only `policy.py`, `receipts.py`, `planner.py`, `retries.py` — no scheduler.\n\n- **Publication end-to-end handling: PARTIAL.** `pubmed.py` provides `build_pubmed_nct_search_url` and `parse_pubmed_efetch_xml` plus `classify_pubmed_records` and `assess_key_field_coverage` (`:262-299`). These are pure helpers; **no executable pipeline invokes them on live data**. There is no `cli.py` research handler that calls `fetch_pubmed_*`, and `fetch_ctgov_condition` is the only `fetch_*` invokable from the CLI (`cli.py:487-540`).\n\n- **OCR of documents: ABSENT.** Searches for `OCR|ocr|Tesseract|tesseract|pytesseract|easyocr` and `from PIL` returned no executable source-acquisition code. The only OCR-adjacent mention was in review/log artifacts outside `src/`.\n\n- **Browser-based (药智/yaozh) adapters: ABSENT in code.** `application/yaozh_access.py` (439 lines) only persists the answer to \"do you have yaozh access?\" (`YaozhAccessRecord`, `YaozhSessionObservation`, `YaozhRouteAccessReceipt`), plus the credential-safety validators in `_safe_observation` (lines 132-163). The runtime store file path is `state/yaozh-route-access/*.json`, but **no browser** (Playwright, Camoufox, requests-html, etc.) is imported anywhere in `src/`. The project's workspace rules (`AGENTS.md`) further state yaozh browser adapters must not appear in the v1 install bundle.\n\n### B4. Route planner (`planner.py` and `policy.py`) — required route enforcement\n\n`/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/sources/planner.py` is **purely a state-machine model class.** It defines:\n\n- `RouteCompletion` (`:19-24`) and `RouteCompletionState` (`COMPLETED` / `NOT_APPLICABLE` / `ACCESS_BLOCKED`, `:13-16`).\n- `RouteProgress` (`:27-111`) with `record_attempt(...)` (`:38-43`) and `complete(...)` (`:45-111`). `.complete(...)` cross-checks progress against an `EvidenceAuditBundle` from `sources/receipts.py` and may require `recovery_exhaustion: RecoveryExhaustionProof` for `not_found` terminals.\n- `HistoricalCutoffAssessment` / `assess_historical_source` (`:114-200`).\n\nThere is **no `RoutePlanner` class**, no executor, no per-source dispatcher. The file is consumed by `_load_scientific_review_request` / `verify_receipt_issuance` (receipt validation only), not as an active planner.\n\n`/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/sources/policy.py` defines:\n- `SourcePolicy` (`policy.py:109-148`) and `SourceDefinition` (`:92-106`).\n- `SourceDefinition.required_global_baseline: bool` and `required_for_china: bool` (`:97-98`) but no method in `policy.py` returns \"the list of required sources for this indication/jurisdiction\" — only `policy.source(source_id)` and `policy.authority_for(source_id, claim_domain)`.\n\nWhat actually **enforces** \"required routes\" lives outside these two files:\n`/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/domain/research_package.py:1011-1031`\n```python\n1019→        required_route_ids = (*self.closure.global_route_ids, *self.closure.china_route_ids)\n1020→        for route_id in required_route_ids:\n1021→            route = route_by_id[route_id]\n1022→            if route.result_class not in {\n1023→                \"completed\",\n1024→                \"success_with_evidence\",\n1025→                \"not_applicable\",\n1026→                \"access_blocked\",\n1027→                \"access_or_permission_blocked\",\n1028→            }:\n1029→                raise ResearchPackageValidationError(\n1030→                    f\"必查路线未完成：{route_id}（{route.result_class}）\"\n1031→                )\n```\ni.e. enforcement is **at the research-package gate**, not in the planner. The planner only records attempts and produces an `EvidenceAuditBundle`; the runner is whatever populates `closure.global_route_ids` and `closure.china_route_ids`.\n\nRequired sources per `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/policies/sources/source-policy-v1.yaml`:\n- `clinicaltrials_gov` — `required_global_baseline: true`\n- `cde` — `required_for_china: true`\n- `chinadrugtrials` — `required_for_china: true`\n- `dxy_drug_assistant` — `required_for_china: true`\n\nThese are listed in the policy YAML but the file does not enforce them; enforcement comes from whatever the `ResearchPackage.closure` says was performed, validated by the gate at `research_package.py:1019`. **The policy flags indicate requiredness; the planner has no executable loop over them.**\n\n### B5. Tests / artifacts proving real end-to-end acquisition\n\nReal live acquisition path that the product commits to:\n\n- `cli.py:487-540` `_research_fetch_ctgov_handler` → `fetch_ctgov_condition` → `derive_ctgov_records` → `ContentAddressedStore` → receipt JSON.\n\nWhat is actually present in tests:\n\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/tests/integration/sources/test_ctgov_fetch.py` — all 10 test invocations use `transport=Pages([...])`/`transport=transport` (synthetic). No hit on the real `clinicaltrials.gov` API. Sample transport, lines 22-33:\n  ```python\n  22→\n  23→class Pages:\n  24→    def __init__(self, payloads: list[dict[str, object] | Exception]) -> None:\n  25→        self.payloads = iter(payloads)\n  ...\n  28→    def __call__(self, url: str, timeout: float, max_bytes: int) -> HttpPage:\n  33→        return HttpPage(200, \"application/json\", json.dumps(value).encode(), url)\n  ```\n\n- PNHandicap fixtures: `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/fixtures/positive/b-pnh/inputs/report-data.json` — bundled JSON, not a live fetch. References to PNH (`apply-cohort`, `appoint-cohort`), `nct04558918`, `nct04820530`, and SCORAD/IGA across renderer code are **string lookups in archived fixture data**, not live acquisition results. `tests/reports/b/test_r13_semantic_grouping.py:18,115-195` explicitly does `load_report_b_data(PNH_DATA)`.\n\n- Other indicators (IgAN / 189 / atopic): same pattern — they live in:\n  - `src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/report_b.py` (label maps only, no fetcher),\n  - `src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/report_c.py` (label maps),\n  - `src/ci_workflow/renderers/pdf_native/projections/c.py:156-157` (translation table),\n  - `tools/rebuild_atopic_dermatitis_package.py` (offline rebuilder for fixture data).\n\n**Net verdict on B5:** No test or artifact in the repository proves a real end-to-end acquisition. The closest thing to \"real\" is the production cli entry `_research_fetch_ctgov_handler`, which *can* hit `clinicaltrials.gov/api/v2/studies`, but no recorded run-output (logs, receipts) in the repo shows it having been driven against live data; all tests use synthetic `transport=Pages(...)` and all fixtures are offline JSON files.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**Question A:** `SemanticGroupingProposal` is a frozen candidate-only carrier (status literal `\"proposal\"`); produced in no production code path (only in tests as `synthetic-model`); consumed by the report B renderer (`report_b.py:2883`) as a merge-or-veto signal on rows already bucketed by `_semantic_group_key`. `issue_review_receipt` (`review_issuer.py:330`) and `promote_rendered_candidate` (`scientific_review_transition.py:646`) act on the **whole portal**, not on individual proposals — there is no per-proposal candidate→approved transition. P3.1 (`clinical_unit`), P3.2 (`time_policy`), P3.4 (a typed `Unresolved` state on clinical facts), P3.5 (a typed `not_applicable`/`unknown` on `ClinicalConstructObservation`/`FactDisclosureState`) are absent; `time_window_band`/`time_window_compatible` is the only time-domain concept present.\n\n**Question B:** Only `ctgov_fetch.py` ships network code (urllib.request, single query shape `query.cond`, paginated). `pubmed.py` provides XML parse and URL builder only; `regulators.py` and `company.py` are validation-only; `china_registries.py` and `authoritative_wechat.py` are validation-only. No historical/as-of reconstruction; no OCR code; no browser adapter code (yaozh is just an access-record store). `planner.py` is a state machine, not an executable planner; required routes are gated by `research_package.py:1019-1031`, not by `planner.py` or `policy.py`. All fetch tests use synthetic `transport=Pages(...)`; all fixtures (`fixtures/positive/b-pnh`, `c-atopic-dermatitis`) are bundled JSON; no repo artifact proves a live end-to-end acquisition."}],"model":"minimax-m3","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":150263,"output_tokens":5664,"cache_creation_input_tokens":437,"cache_read_input_tokens":149826,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":"call_02_7faHW2LQzop1uyMQUW6r9666","_requestId":"01a08c80d6917d96bda67b4c7a4cb76d","_messageId":"01a08c82a48a72759bae4153b3c8b712","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a08c80d6917d96bda67b4c7a4cb76d","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a08c82a48a72759bae4153b3c8b712","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a08c82a48a72759bae4153b3c8b712","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a08c82-a48a-7275-9bae-4154ba3e106a","traceparent":"00-a4b4af999c08dd6458b96ec034bb4fe0-e2f7c4948accacf5-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a08c80-51fc-7e4d-8c44-75c5d8fe8dd6,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a08c8052637ef99d54eb1364f5e9f1"},"__timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:09:55.263Z"}
