:|---|\n| `_semantic_token` | 273 | Token normalization that strips `<≥/≤/％>` and lowercases — used as the canonicalization primitive for *all* downstream concept matching. |\n| `_concept_family` | 283 | Builds equivalence sets of clinical concept aliases (e.g. `age` ⇔ `baseline_age`). |\n| `_BASELINE_CONCEPT_FAMILY_ORDER` (const) | 287 | Hard-coded medical-concept ordering for baseline buckets. |\n| `_alias_lookup` | 296 | Builds reverse alias maps; raises on collision — implements domain-specific conflict detection. |\n| `_CLINICAL_CONCEPT_GROUPS` (const) | 310 | Hand-curated clinical concept alias tables (EASI75/90, IGA 0/1, haemoglobin sustained increase, etc.) — domain knowledge embedded as data. |\n| `_unknown_semantic_key` | 745 | Names unknown clinical concepts. |\n| `_controlled_concept` | 750 | Maps raw values to controlled vocabularies; falls back to \"concept not listed\". |\n| `_canonical_statistical_form` | 771 | Decides whether a measurement is `event_rate`, `response_rate`, `proportion`, `count`, etc., based on domain, concept, and unit. |\n| `_canonical_population` | 806 | Maps population text to a canonical population label. |\n| `_canonical_arm_role` | 815 | Decides whether an arm is `treatment`, `control`, `single_arm`, or `unknown` via substring markers (e.g. `control`, `placebo`, `对照`, `安慰剂`). |\n| `_time_band` | 835 | Buckets timepoints into `baseline`, `treatment_period`, `follow_up`, `study_period`, parses numeric timepoint strings, and converts day/week/month/year to weeks. |\n| `_semantic_projection` | 882 | Picks the right field name for a concept per domain (`clinical_concept`, `construct_id`, `endpoint_family_id`, `standard_term`, etc.). |\n| `_semantic_domain_for_page` | 2574 | Maps page id → domain (`efficacy` / `safety` / `baseline` / `disposition` / `generic`). |\n| `_records_with_semantics` | 2586 | Backfills the R13 semantic dimensions on legacy rows. |\n| `_chart_series_key` / `_chart_series_label` | 2610 / 2616 | Decide whether rows are series-distinguishable. |\n| `_group_title` | 2634 | Composes Chinese group titles using clinical-concept / statistic / time-band / population labels. |\n| `_project_scientific_groups` | 2748 | Projects clinical group buckets into chart payloads. |\n| `_sorted_bucket` | 2835 | Sort key that gives `treatment` priority over `control` — clinical arm-role ordering. |\n| `_baseline_bucket_sort_key` | 2944 | Enforces the order in `_BASELINE_CONCEPT_FAMILY_ORDER`. |\n| `_bucket_spans_trials` | 2952 | Decides cross-trial flag (true when ≥ 2 distinct `trial_id`). |\n| `_filter_dimensions` / `_filter_groups` | 3142 / 3190 | Filter logic driven by arm role and population. |\n\n### Domain-decision verdictThese are **not pure formatting helpers**. The file's docstring (lines 1–8) states the renderer is \"deliberately an adapter\" and \"does not calculate comparisons, proportions, denominators, or disclosure states in the browser.\" However, this file embeds substantial clinical/medical decision logic locally:\n\n- It maintains a hand-curated clinical-concept alias table (`_CLINICAL_CONCEPT_GROUPS`, ~lines 310–744) listing EASI75/90/IGA0–1/hemoglobin-response aliases in both English and Chinese — domain knowledge.\n- It hard-codes arm-role and time-band classification rules (`_canonical_arm_role`, `_time_band`) that decide whether two arms are comparable.\n- `_cross_trial_groups` explicitly decides whether records can be merged across trials, gates on semantic completeness, and demotes unknown-key buckets to source-specific series (see comment at lines 2874–2881).\n- `_canonical_statistical_form` decides statistical-form equivalence (event_rate vs response_rate vs proportion vs count) using domain, concept, and unit.\n- `_semantic_group_key` is a multi-axis clinical concept key that incorporates `semantic_definition`, `semantic_direction`, `semantic_estimand`, `semantic_denominator`, `semantic_analysis_set`, `semantic_analysis_form`, `semantic_instrument_or_scale` — all clinical-adjudication axes.\n\n### Representative snippets (each is local to `report_b.py`)\n\nSnippet A — clinical alias lookup with conflict detection (lines 296–307):\n```python\ndef _alias_lookup(groups: Mapping[str, Sequence[str]]) -> dict[str, str]:\n    result: dict[str, str] = {}\n    for canonical, aliases in groups.items():\n        for alias in (canonical, *aliases):\n            token = _semantic_token(alias)\n            if not token:\n                continue\n            existing = result.get(token)\n            if existing is not None and existing != canonical:\n                raise RuntimeError(f\"B 类临床别名冲突：{token}\")\n            result[token] = canonical\n    return result\n```\n\nSnippet B — arm-role adjudication with substring markers (lines 815–832):\n```python\ndef _canonical_arm_role(value: Any) -> tuple[str, str]:\n    candidates = (value,)\n    for candidate in candidates:\n        token = _semantic_token(candidate)\n        canonical = _ARM_ROLE_ALIASES.get(token)\n        if canonical is not None:\n            return canonical, {\n                \"treatment\": \"治疗组\",\n                \"control\": \"对照组\",\n                \"single_arm\": \"单臂\",\n            }[canonical]\n        if any(\n            marker in token for marker in (\"control\", \"placebo\", \"comparator\", \"对照\", \"安慰剂\")\n        ):\n            return \"control\", \"对照组\"\n        if any(marker in token for marker in (\"treat\", \"intervention\", \"active\", \"治疗\", \"干预\")):\n            return \"treatment\", \"治疗组\"\n    return \"unknown\", \"组别未列示\"\n```\n\nSnippet C — cross-trial comparability decision in `_cross_trial_groups` (lines 2861–2882):\n```python\ndef _cross_trial_groups(\n    records: Sequence[tuple[dict[str, Any], Any]],\n    *, page_id: str, domain: str, include_time: bool,\n    chart_type: str | None = None,\n    semantic_proposals: Sequence[SemanticGroupingProposal] = (),\n) -> tuple[dict[str, Any], ...]:\n    buckets: dict[tuple[str, ...], list[tuple[dict[str, Any], Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for item in records:\n        row = item[0]\n        key = _semantic_group_key(row, include_time=include_time)\n        if any(semantic_value_is_unknown(value) for value in key):\n            # Retain source observations, but unknown axes cannot license cross-trial comparison.\n            # Without a trial identity even a within-trial descriptive grouping is unproven.\n            key += (\n                \"source-specific\",\n                _text(row.get(\"product_id\")),\n                _text(row.get(\"trial_id\"), _text(row.get(\"row_id\"))),\n            )\n        buckets[key].append(item)\n merged = proposed_semantic_buckets(tuple(buckets.values()), semantic_proposals)\n```\n\nSnippet D — clinical-statistic-form equivalence rule (lines 771–792):\n```python\ndef _canonical_statistical_form(value, *, domain, concept, unit=None, ...):\n    if domain == \"efficacy\" and concept == \"breakthrough_hemolysis_rate\":\n        return \"event_rate\", \"事件发生率（越低越好）\"\n    canonical = _STATISTICAL_FORM_LOOKUP.get(_semantic_token(value))\n    if canonical is not None:\n        return canonical, _STATISTICAL_FORM_LABELS[canonical]\n    unit_token = _text(unit).strip().casefold().replace(\"％\", \"%\")\n    if domain == \"safety\":\n        return \"event_rate\", _STATISTICAL_FORM_LABELS[\"event_rate\"]\n    if domain == \"efficacy\":\n        if concept.endswith(\"_response\") or concept == \"hemoglobin_response_without_transfusion\":\n            return \"response_rate\", _STATISTICAL_FORM_LABELS[\"response_rate\"]\n        if unit_token in {\"%\", \"percent\", \"percentage\"}:\n            return \"proportion\", _STATISTICAL_FORM_LABELS[\"proportion\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Does `src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/report_b.py` import from `ci_workflow.reports.b`?\n\n**Yes, partially — but only two narrow submodules of the scientific view layer.** The renderer's imports from `ci_workflow.reports.b` (lines 31–40):\n\n```python\nfrom ci_workflow.reports.b.semantic_contract import (\n    BUBBLE_PRESETS,\n    semantic_value_is_unknown,\n)\nfrom ci_workflow.reports.b.semantic_grouping import (\n    SemanticGroupingProposal,\n    proposed_semantic_buckets,\n    semantic_row_digest,\n    semantic_source_digest,\n)\n```\n\nWhat it does **not** import from `ci_workflow.reports.b`:\n- `reports.b.pages` (3,757 lines) — the matrix view state machinery.\n- `reports.b.safety` (3,333 lines) — `SafetyFactRow`, `SafetyViewSet`, `SafetyHeatmapView`, `SafetyArmComparison`, etc.\n- `reports.b.efficacy` (3,316 lines) — `EfficacyFactRow`, `EfficacyViewSet`, `EfficacyComparison`, `EndpointBasisSet`, etc.\n- `reports.b.baseline_views` (2,052 lines), `reports/b/baseline.py` (882), `reports/b/disposition_views.py` (2,463), `reports/b/disposition.py` (843), `reports/b/contracts.py` (1,028), `reports/b/semantic_contract.py` (414 — only the small subset above).\n\nNet verdict: **the renderer re-implements the majority of the per-domain grouping / classification / clinical-decision logic locally** (see §4 above), pulling only small shared primitives (`semantic_value_is_unknown`, `proposed_semantic_buckets`, `BUBBLE_PRESETS`, `SemanticGroupingProposal`, and two digest helpers) from the scientific view layer. It does not consume the major view-layer classes (`SafetyFactRow`, `EfficacyFactRow`, `MatrixViewState`, etc.) and does not call into `reports.b.pages`, `reports.b.safety`, or `reports.b.efficacy` — those packages' own logic is mirrored by `_semantic_group_key`, `_cross_trial_groups`, `_groups_for_page`, `_canonical_arm_role`, `_canonical_statistical_form`, `_canonical_population`, `_time_band`, and the local `_CLINICAL_CONCEPT_GROUPS` alias table.\n\nOther renderer-side imports of note (full list):\n- `ci_workflow.domain.enums` (FactDisclosureState, ReportKind)\n- `ci_workflow.domain.evidence` (EvidenceLocator)\n- `ci_workflow.domain.ids` (stable_id)\n- `ci_workflow.qc.browser` (route_to_site_path, site_directory_digest)\n- `ci_workflow.reports.common.evidence_view` (EvidenceField, EvidenceObservationKind, EvidenceView, etc.)\n- `ci_workflow.reports.common.page_registry` (PageRegistry, ReportCatalog, StaticPage)\n- `ci_workflow.reports.common.view_state` (ReportRow)\n- `ci_workflow.storage.manifest_store`, `ci_workflow.storage.render_transaction`, `ci_workflow.storage.snapshot_store`\n- Sibling renderers: `.builder`, `.evidence_drawer`, `.report_a` (for `EfficacyRow`, `ReportAPortalData`, `SafetyRow`, `TrialRow`, `_git_commit`).\n\n[Agent ID: agent-b9636819cebf4e1c]"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a08c8052637ef99d54eb1364f5e9f1","_messageId":"01a08c80a83f772c9ee964583c8c4913","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a08c8052637ef99d54eb1364f5e9f1","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a08c80a83f772c9ee964583c8c4913","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a08c80a83f772c9ee964583c8c4913","traceparent":"00-a4b4af999c08dd6458b96ec034bb4fe0-e2f7c4948accacf5-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a08c80-51fc-7e4d-8c44-75c5d8fe8dd6,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a08c8052637ef99d54eb1364f5e9f1"},"__timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:09:55.263Z"}
{"type":"user","uuid":"01a08c83-1242-702b-9318-623cc5b85ee0","session_id":"01a08c80-51fc-7e4d-8c44-75c5d8fe8dd6","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_01_Lu0OJcaEYTbMXclQKXlC2249","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I cannot create a plan file because the `Write` tool is not available in this context. Since your request was a READ-ONLY investigation with a markdown report as the deliverable, I will provide the findings directly below.\n\n---\n\n# Portal Static Asset Duplication Investigation Report\n\n## 1. File listing, byte size, line count\n\nThe `bash` tool is denied in this session, so byte sizes and line counts were derived from the JSON manifests plus reading each file's tail. Where bash cannot run, sizes from the governance manifest are authoritative.\n\n### `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/assets/portal/`\n\n| File | Bytes (per `manifest.json`) | Lines |\n|---|---|---|\n| `charts.js` | 63,109 | 1,822 |\n| `evidence-drawer.css` | 9,524 | 458 |\n| `evidence-drawer.js` | 28,555 | 827 |\n| `manifest.json` | (37 lines) | 37 |\n| `portal.css` | 49,960 | 1,558 |\n| `portal.js` | 40,204 | 1,241 |\n\nAbsolute paths:\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/assets/portal/charts.js`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/assets/portal/evidence-drawer.css`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/assets/portal/evidence-drawer.js`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/assets/portal/manifest.json`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/assets/portal/portal.css`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/assets/portal/portal.js`\n\n### `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/`\n\n| File | Bytes | Lines |\n|---|---|---|\n| `charts.js` | (matches manifest: 63,109) | 1,822 |\n| `cms-logo.svg` | (not in portal manifest; brand manifest) | — |\n| `echarts.min.js` | 1,121,883 (manifest value) | — |\n| `evidence-drawer.css` | (matches manifest: 9,524) | 458 |\n| `evidence-drawer.js` | (matches manifest: 28,555) | 827 |\n| `portal.css` | (matches manifest: 49,960) | 1,558 |\n| `portal.js` | (matches manifest: 40,204) | 1,241 |\n| `report-a.css` | in-module only | — |\n| `report-a.js` | in-module only | — |\n| `report-b.css` | in-module only | — |\n| `report-b.js` | in-module only | — |\n| `report-c.css` | in-module only | — |\n| `report-c.js` | in-module only | — |\n\nAbsolute paths:\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/cms-logo.svg`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/charts.js`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/echarts.min.js`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/evidence-drawer.css`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/evidence-drawer.js`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/portal.css`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/portal.js`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/report-a.css`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/report-a.js`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/report-b.css`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/report-b.js`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/report-c.css`\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/report-c.js`\n\n### Files present in only ONE location\n\n**Only in `assets/portal/` (root):**\n- `manifest.json`\n\n**Only in `src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/` (in-module):**\n- `cms-logo.svg`\n- `echarts.min.js`\n- `report-a.css`\n- `report-a.js`\n- `report-b.css`\n- `report-b.js`\n- `report-c.css`\n- `report-c.js`\n\n**Present in BOTH locations:**\n- `charts.js`\n- `evidence-drawer.css`\n- `evidence-drawer.js`\n- `portal.css`\n- `portal.js`\n\n## 2. Byte-identical verdict (right now)\n\n`bash`/`shasum` cannot be run, so byte-identity was assessed by (a) reading the head lines and tail lines of both copies and (b) comparing the line counts to the manifest's declared `bytes` field. All five shared files reach the same `bytes` value the manifest records for the root copy and the same terminating line number on both sides.\n\n| File | Root lines | Module lines | Head match | Tail match | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `charts.js` | 1,822 | 1,822 | yes (lines 1-9) | yes (last lines) | identical |\n| `portal.css` | 1,558 | 1,558 | yes (lines 1-10) | yes (last 5 lines close on `}`) | identical |\n| `portal.js` | 1,241 | 1,241 | yes (lines 1-5) | yes (last lines: `})();`) | identical |\n| `evidence-drawer.css` | 458 | 458 | yes (lines 1-5) | yes (closes at line 458 `}`) | identical |\n| `evidence-drawer.js` | 827 | 827 | yes (lines 1-5) | yes (closes at line 826 `})();`) | identical |\n\nNote: this is a structural / line-count + sample check, not a SHA-256 check. The test guardrails in section 4 below do the actual SHA-256 / byte-equality assertions and they are the source of truth.\n\n## 3. `resolve_portal_asset` resolution order\n\nSource: `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/builder.py`\n\nThe asset module location and digest constants are defined at lines 117-121:\n\n```python\n117→_MODULE_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n118→_MODULE_ASSETS_DIR = _MODULE_DIR / \"assets\"\n119→_OFFICIAL_LOGO_SHA256 = \"8d16d3ae8353dd31f46a50d401e66f9e62af40be6cc42cdf5050866a4e6e1cae\"\n120→_ECHARTS_BUNDLE_SHA256 = \"b66b25aeb4df84e33199dc21694014d336d222cbd9deb0e5a7c14bd6aa0d0fd0\"\n121→_ECHARTS_BUNDLE_NAME = \"echarts.min.js\"\n```\n\nHelper `_repo_assets_root()` (lines 132-141) walks up parent dirs looking for an `assets/portal` + `assets/brand` pair to find the editable-checkout repo root.\n\nThe actual `resolve_portal_asset` (lines 144-170):\n\n```python\n144→def resolve_portal_asset(name: str) -> Path:\n145→    \"\"\"Resolve a portal static asset for copy into a generated site.\"\"\"\n146→    module_candidate = _MODULE_ASSETS_DIR / name\n147→    if module_candidate.is_file():\n148→        return module_candidate\n149→\n150→    repo_assets = _repo_assets_root()\n151→    if repo_assets is not None:\n152→        if name in {\n153→            \"portal.css\",\n154→            \"portal.js\",\n155→            \"charts.js\",\n156→            \"evidence-drawer.css\",\n157→            \"evidence-drawer.js\",\n158→        }:\n159→            repo_candidate = repo_assets / \"portal\" / name\n160→            if repo_candidate.is_file():\n161→                return repo_candidate\n162→        if name in {\"cms-logo.svg\", \"logo.svg\"}:\n163→            brand = repo_assets / \"brand\" / \"cms-logo.svg\"\n164→            if brand.is_file():\n165→                return brand\n166→\n167→    raise PortalBuildError(\n168→        f\"Portal asset '{name}' not found in packaged module assets \"\n169→        f\"({_MODULE_ASSETS_DIR}) or repository assets tree\"\n170→    )\n```\n\nResolution order, in plain English:\n\n1. **First** check the in-module copy at `src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/<name>`. If that file exists, return it. No hash check is done here (only `_ECHARTS_BUNDLE_SHA256` and `_OFFICIAL_LOGO_SHA256` are pinned, both via separate functions).\n2. **Fallback** only if the in-module copy is missing: scan for a repository `assets/` root via `_repo_assets_root()`.\n   - For names in the allow-list `{portal.css, portal.js, charts.js, evidence-drawer.css, evidence-drawer.js}`: try `repo_assets/portal/<name>`. This is the only path that can resolve to `assets/portal/` (repo root).\n   - For `{cms-logo.svg, logo.svg}`: try `repo_assets/brand/cms-logo.svg`.\n3. **Failure mode**: if neither exists, raise `PortalBuildError` (a `RuntimeError` subclass defined at line 109). The error message lists both candidate roots so the failure is actionable.\n\nCrucially: there is **no fallback path** for `echarts.min.js`, `report-a.js`, `report-b.js`, `report-c.js`, or any of the `report-*.css` files — those live exclusively in the in-module tree (and `resolve_echarts_bundle` at line 173 explicitly refuses any repo fallback and additionally verifies the SHA-256).\n\n`build_portal()` (lines 240-250) only ever passes these names to `resolve_portal_asset`: `portal.css`, `portal.js`, `charts.js`, `evidence-drawer.css`, `evidence-drawer.js`, plus the logo via `resolve_logo_src()` and `echarts.min.js` via `resolve_echarts_bundle()`. `report-a.js/css`, `report-b.js/css`, `report-c.js/css` are not loaded by `build_portal()`; the grep found no Python consumer for them either (they are portal-internal assets used by their respective `report_a.py`/`report_b.py`/`report_c.py` page renderers — not pulled through `resolve_portal_asset`).\n\n### Is `assets/portal/manifest.json` consumed anywhere in Python?\n\nYes — exactly one place:\n\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/cli.py:163-185`, in `_verify_asset_manifests`, invoked from `verify_package()` at line 268 and from `main()` (line 340). The function reads `assets/portal/manifest.json` (line 168), iterates `portal[\"files\"]` (line 172), and calls `_verify_digest()` on each entry against the `assets/portal/<name>` or `assets/third-party/echarts/<echarts_source>` path. This is a hash-and-size verification path, not an asset-loader path.\n\nThere is no other `manifest.json` consumer for the portal manifest. `renderers/portal/builder.py` does NOT touch it.\n\n## 4. Tests that guard the duplication/sync\n\n### Direct byte-equality / SHA-256 guards\n\n`/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/tests/browser/test_portal_shell.py`, `TestPortalShell.test_packaged_assets_match_repo_and_official_logo` (lines 455-479):\n- Reads `assets/portal/portal.css` and `src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/portal.css` and asserts `read_bytes() == read_bytes()`.\n- Same for `portal.js`.\n- Asserts `assets/brand/cms-logo.svg` == `src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/cms-logo.svg` (this is a brand-vs-module comparison, not portal-vs-module).\n- Asserts SHA-256 of `portal.css` and `portal.js` matches `manifest.json[\"files\"][...][\"sha256\"]`.\n- Asserts SHA-256 of `cms-logo.svg` equals `OFFICIAL_LOGO_SHA256`.\n\nWhat this test covers: **portal.css, portal.js, cms-logo.svg**. It does NOT cover `charts.js`, `evidence-drawer.css`, `evidence-drawer.js`, `echarts.min.js`.\n\n`/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/tests/browser/test_evidence_drawer.py`, `test_packaged_drawer_assets_mirrored_and_manifested` (lines 192-205):\n- For `evidence-drawer.js` and `evidence-drawer.css`: asserts `assets/portal/<name>.read_bytes() == src/.../assets/<name>.read_bytes()`.\n- Asserts `manifest[\"files\"][name][\"sha256\"]` matches SHA-256 of the in-module copy.\n- Asserts `manifest[\"files\"][name][\"bytes\"]` matches `packaged.stat().st_size`.\n\nWhat this test covers: **evidence-drawer.js, evidence-drawer.css**. It does NOT cover `charts.js` or `echarts.min.js`.\n\n### Manifest-content guard\n\n`/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/cli.py:_verify_asset_manifests` (lines 163-185) is invoked by `verify_package` (line 268). It iterates `manifest[\"files\"]` and `_verify_digest()` against `assets/portal/<name>` (line 176) or `assets/third-party/echarts/echarts.min.js` (line 171/176). The manifest lists six files: `portal.css`, `portal.js`, `charts.js`, `evidence-drawer.js`, `evidence-drawer.css`, `echarts.min.js`. This is the only place that hashes `charts.js` and `echarts.min.js` in the install bundle.\n\n### Test coverage gap\n\n| File | Portal↔module byte-equality test | Manifest hash/size test |\n|---|---|---|\n| `portal.css` | YES (`test_portal_shell.py`) | YES (`test_portal_shell.py`) |\n| `portal.js` | YES (`test_portal_shell.py`) | YES (`test_portal_shell.py`) |\n| `evidence-drawer.js` | YES (`test_evidence_drawer.py`) | YES (`test_evidence_drawer.py`) |\n| `evidence-drawer.css` | YES (`test_evidence_drawer.py`) | YES (`test_evidence_drawer.py`) |\n| `charts.js` | NO direct byte-equality test | YES via `_verify_asset_manifests` |\n| `echarts.min.js` | NO direct byte-equality test | YES via `_verify_asset_manifests` |\n| `cms-logo.svg` | YES (`test_portal_shell.py`, but as brand-vs-module) | YES (`_verify_asset_manifests` brand path) |\n\n`charts.js` and `echarts.min.js` have no portal↔module byte-equality test. They are protected only by the manifest hash check, which is applied to the root copy (`assets/portal/charts.js`, `assets/third-party/echarts/echarts.min.js`), not the in-module copies — see the resolution order at line 152-161 which means the in-module copy is consumed by the wheel and is NOT what `_verify_asset_manifests` hashes.\n\n### Other drift-related tests (NOT portal-asset sync)\n\nThe search for `drift`, `sync` etc. surfaced many tests for *portal runtime behaviour*, not portal-asset duplication:\n\n- `tests/integration/test_scientific_review_transition.py:611` `test_portal_byte_drift_on_republish_fails_closed` — runtime republish drift, not asset duplication.\n- `tests/integration/test_scientific_review_transition.py:636`, `:799` — same theme.\n- `tests/fixtures/task44-chart-table-sync/render_fixture.py:190` reads `repo_root / \"assets/portal/charts.js\"` (root copy) while `echarts_src = packaged / \"echarts.min.js\"` is the in-module copy — this fixture mixes sources, not enforcing identity.\n- All other `drift` matches are about checkpoint replay, fixture catalogs, host-smoke bundles, manual inbox content, source-text derivation, etc. — none guard the asset duplication.\n\n## 5. Packaging config\n\n`/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/pyproject.toml`:\n\n- Lines 20-22: `[build-system] requires = [\"uv_build>=0.11.7,<0.12\"]`, `build-backend = \"uv_build\"`. There is no `[tool.uv.build-backend]` `module-root`, `package-data`, or `data-files` override beyond line 36-37 (`module-name = \"ci_workflow\"`). The `uv_build` backend auto-includes Python and recognized resource files under the module root `src/ci_workflow/` — meaning `src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/*.js`, `*.css`, `cms-logo.svg`, `echarts.min.js`, `*.svg` ship inside the wheel.\n- `MANIFEST.in` does NOT exist.\n- `setup.py` does NOT exist.\n\n`/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/package-manifest.json`:\n\n- `components.assets` (lines 94-98) lists three repo-root manifests: `assets/brand/manifest.json`, `assets/portal/manifest.json`, `assets/third-party/echarts/manifest.json`. These are paths relative to the candidate install root, NOT inside the wheel. They are copied into the bundle by the install tooling.\n- `components.schemas` (lines 34-79), `components.policies` (lines 80-87), `components.contracts` (lines 88-93), `components.migrations` (lines 99-110) — none of these reference `assets/portal/` files (other than the manifest itself).\n- `verify_package()` in `cli.py` (line 197) validates `package-manifest.json` against `schemas/package-manifest.schema.json` and enforces the constraints at lines 211-248 (including `release_scope == \"site_html_v1\"`, `formats == [\"html\"]`, internal-skill closure).\n\nThe relevant install-bundle logic lives in `tools/install_bundle.py`, `tools/build_bundle.py`, and `tools/verify_bundle.py` (referenced in CLI at line 340). Per `package-manifest.json`'s `components.assets`, only the three repo-root manifests are explicitly enumerated — the actual asset files referenced by those manifests (`portal.css`, `portal.js`, `charts.js`, `evidence-drawer.*`, `echarts.min.js`, `cms-logo.svg`) are referenced indirectly via the manifest contents.\n\n**What ships in the v1 install bundle:**\n- Inside the wheel: `src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/` (all 13 files, including `portal.css`, `portal.js`, `charts.js`, `evidence-drawer.*`, `echarts.min.js`, `cms-logo.svg`, and the `report-{a,b,c}.{js,css}` files).\n- Copied alongside the wheel from the repo root: `assets/brand/manifest.json`, `assets/portal/manifest.json`, `assets/third-party/echarts/manifest.json` (and the asset files those manifests reference at `assets/brand/cms-logo.svg`, `assets/third-party/echarts/echarts.min.js`, `assets/portal/{portal.css,portal.js,charts.js,evidence-drawer.js,evidence-drawer.css}`).\n\n**Verdict on which copy `build_portal` reads in a wheel install:** the in-module copy at `src/ci_workflow/renderers/portal/assets/` — see the resolution order in section 3. The repo-root `assets/portal/` is only consulted when the in-module copy is missing (an editable-checkout fallback).\n\n## 6. Are `assets/html-ppt/`, `assets/brand/`, `assets/third-party/echarts/` referenced by v1 HTML-only runtime code, or only by excluded surfaces?\n\nGrep across `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src`:\n\n### `assets/html-ppt/`\n\nOnly one source reference:\n- `/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow/src/ci_workflow/renderers/html_ppt/assets.py:15`